    <h2>About the Work</h2>

    <p>
      This interactive black-and-white web narrative tells a story about
      a couple reuniting after a war. Instead of presenting the story as
      one continuous page, it divides text and images into frames.
      Visitors click through the frames and make choices about what they
      see next, so navigating the website becomes part of experiencing
      the story.
    </p>

    <h2>Connection to the Exhibition</h2>

    <p>
      Lialina’s work changes the usual reading experience. The viewer has
      to interact with the page to piece together the narrative. This
      connects to the exhibition’s larger idea that early net art made
      the website’s structure and the viewer’s actions part of the artwork.
    </p>

